From 99b9361c842c76259b4c4c4324826838599e4c43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:31:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] zgx: text below 2x is drawn for the screen's subpixels, as
 ClearType draws it

Zeron's text on a ~96 dpi Windows screen read blurry beside Windows' own:
greyscale coverage leaves each stem over two columns at part strength
(Geist hints vertically only), which zgx#1516's whole-pixel places and
firmed edges can't do better. Windows' text is sharp because ClearType
covers each subpixel apart.

apps/zgx's zgx moves to hoangvu12/zgx 0d60ffa19 (branch
nightly-lcd-0d60ffa1): main's pin, zeronsh/zgx b9e744ddd, with two commits
on it. Glyphs keyed CacheKeyFlags::LCD are swash subpixel masks, drawn by a
dual-source pipeline (Shading::Lcd) that blends each channel by its own
coverage. Only into an opaque window's own target, below 2x, off macOS, on
a device with dual-source blending: frosted or transparent windows and
isolated layers keep greyscale, since their pixels are blended again. The
desktop host follows Windows' ClearType setting (on, RGB or BGR) and reads
it again on a settings change; ZGX_LCD_TEXT=0, rgb or bgr overrides it.

The second commit makes it show in a Windows window: LCD text turned
itself off wherever a frame could present in a single pass (every Windows
window), so a frame with LCD glyphs is now drawn into the target and
presented after; and a glass window whose glass is dropped is cleared
opaque in its theme's background.

Zeron's main window is made with glass, and its themes' backgrounds are
translucent (72-80%), so even with frosted glass off its text stayed grey.
Now the glass is kept only while something shows through it (ui/app.luau
asks `window.glass` with ds/material's see_through(); src/main.rs sets or
drops zeron_glass on app.luau's windows), and a solid window's background
is its theme's with the alpha dropped (ds/glass_tint `opaque`, used by
ds/material's solid theme). These go with the zgx pin in one patch: on a
zgx without the second commit, a window whose glass is dropped would clear
transparent.

Checked in the real app on Windows (1080p, 110%): chat text's edges went
from 0 coloured pixels of 3045 to 2812 of 2932, the spread of Discord's
ClearType text beside it.
